# Edge Case: Tautological If Without Else
# This file demonstrates an if conditional with True as the condition and
# no else branch. Per the specification, a tautologically true condition
# makes the else unnecessary — there is no code path where a value would
# not be produced.
#
# If the analyzer recognizes True as a tautology, this should parse and
# analyze successfully despite having no else. If not, it will produce a
# completeness error.
#
# Expected behavior: Should be valid per spec (tautologically true condition
# makes else unnecessary). Document actual behavior when verified.

concepts
    Region = [Values[North, South]]
    Unit = [Values[Each]]
    Day = [Values[Monday]]

units
    Region = Region
    Unit = Unit
    Day = Day

types
    NumberType = Number()

measures
    input_a = NumberType(unit=Unit)
    Daily = Interval(unit=Day)

connectors
    data_a = dimensions [Region] grain Daily celltype input_a

metrics
    tautology_metric
        inputs
            metric input_a
        calculate
            if True
                input_a
            end if
